                "FUNCTION GTPase involved in the 5-carboxymethylaminomethyl modification (mnm(5)s(2)U34) of the wobble uridine base in mitochondrial tRNAs. Involved in the expression of cytochrome c oxidase subunit 1 (COX1). Works in association with the small subunit of mitoribosomes.SUBUNIT Forms a heterodimer with MTO1.INTERACTION Present with 768 molecules/cell in log phase SD medium.SIMILARITY Belongs to the TRAFAC class TrmE-Era-EngA-EngB-Septin-like GTPase superfamily. TrmE GTPase family.";
